.TH WELLUSB 1 "August 2026" "wellusb 2.0" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
Wellusb \- E n u m e r a t e s   U S B   d e v i c e s ,   m a t c h i n g   v e n d o r / d e v i c e   I D s   a g a i n s t   t h e   h w d a t a
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellusb
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellusb
.PP
Enumerates USB devices, matching vendor/device IDs against the hwdata
usb.ids database, and classifies each device (hubs, keyboards, mice,
gamepads, printers, storage, audio, network, cameras) combining the
device class with the set of interface classes for composite devices.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1)
